odot v4.5.dev (ced7e2c03) - macOS Sonoma (14.5.0) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M1 Pro (Apple7) - Apple M1 Pro (10 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nCurrently, the `TabContainer` class has a theme stylebox called `tabbar_background`. With most other UI elements, the rendered element is resized to respect the stylebox's set margins, however this theme item does not respect that / have that behavior.\n\n<img width=\"751\" alt=\"Margins not being respected\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/47facfd6-f2de-4869-b9b0-834bd4b994a3\" />\n\nExpectation: There is 20px of empty space (just showing the stylebox) on the left, right, top, and bottom of the TabBar.\n\nThis is a mockup:\n<img width=\"645\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b868638d-9f42-40e3-8d80-a29f799f073d\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a TabContainer\n- Give the TabContainer a theme\n- In that theme, override `tabbar_background` and add a stylebox\n- Change the margins of stylebox to be any number\n- Note how the TabContainer is unaffected.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20217569/MRP.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/